  "courseName": "General Physics I (Mechanics)",
  "estimatedLength": "25 minutes",
  "objectives": [
    "Students will represent a two-dimensional vector by its magnitude and direction, and equivalently by its horizontal and vertical components.",
    "Students will add two or more vectors graphically using the tip-to-tail method and identify the resultant vector.",
    "Students will decompose a vector into components along the x- and y-axes using right-triangle trigonometry.",
    "Students will explain why the horizontal and vertical motions of a projectile are independent of one another.",
    "Students will describe how horizontal and vertical velocity change over the course of projectile flight.",
    "Students will predict how changes in initial launch angle and launch speed affect the trajectory, range, and maximum height of a projectile."
  ],
